monero_c: recover HOST_ABI when CMake throws the cache away.

build_single.sh passes the target triplet as `-DHOST_ABI=<triplet>`, which
lives only in CMakeCache.txt. CMake deletes that cache and silently re-runs
configure whenever a variable it considers structural changes underneath it:

    You have changed variables that require your cache to be deleted.
    Configure will be re-run and you may have to reset some variables.
    The following variables have changed:
    CMAKE_CXX_COMPILER= /monero_c/contrib/depends/_native/bin/aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc

The re-run has no command line to take -D from, so HOST_ABI comes back empty
and the first comparison below degenerates from

    if(${HOST_ABI} STREQUAL "x86_64-w64-mingw32")

to `if(STREQUAL "x86_64-w64-mingw32")`, which is a CMake syntax error:

    CMake Error at CMakeLists.txt:10 (if):
      if given arguments:
        "STREQUAL" "x86_64-w64-mingw32"
      Unknown arguments specified

Observed on aarch64-linux-gnu, mid-`make`, after the first two configures of
the same build directory had already succeeded with the correct value. It is
intermittent, it costs the entire target, and a plain `docker build` has no
retry to absorb it -- the RUN layer is discarded and roughly an hour and a half
of toolchain work goes with it.

Recover the value from the environment. contrib/depends/<triplet>/_source_me
exports HOST with exactly the triplet build_single.sh passes, build_single.sh
sources it before invoking cmake, and the environment is not the cache, so it
survives the deletion that caused the problem.

Deliberately not fixed by quoting the comparisons. `if("" STREQUAL "...")` is
legal and simply false, so quoting would turn a loud syntax error into a silent
misbuild: CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME never set for the Windows and Darwin targets, the
android and linux-gnu link flags dropped. The unquoted forms are left as they
are precisely because they cannot fail quietly, and the else branch below is a
hard error for the same reason.

--- a/monero_libwallet2_api_c/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/monero_libwallet2_api_c/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1,6 +1,22 @@
 cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.5)
 project(${MONERO_FLAVOR}_wallet2_api_c)
 message(STATUS HOST_ABI = ${HOST_ABI})
+
+# -DHOST_ABI lives only in CMakeCache.txt, and CMake deletes the cache and
+# re-runs configure by itself when a structural variable changes. That re-run
+# has no command line, so the value is lost and every comparison below becomes
+# a syntax error. _source_me exports the same triplet as HOST and is
+# environment rather than cache, so it survives.
+if(NOT HOST_ABI)
+    if(DEFINED ENV{HOST})
+        set(HOST_ABI "$ENV{HOST}")
+        message(STATUS "HOST_ABI was empty, recovered from environment: ${HOST_ABI}")
+    else()
+        message(FATAL_ERROR
+            "HOST_ABI is empty and HOST is not in the environment. "
+            "Run this through build_single.sh, which sets both.")
+    endif()
+endif()
 
 set(MD_LIBRARY "")
 
